<title>BELGIUM: EU to clear Iridium satellite communications system.</title>
<headline>EU to clear Iridium satellite communications system.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it planned to clear the Motorola-led Iridium satellite communications system but said it wanted to hear from other interested parties before making a final decision.</p>
<p>The Commission started a probe in May 1995 into the project, which is scheduled to begin commercial operations by October 1, 1998. Apart from Motorola, Iridium is owned by 16 other investors including Germany's Vebacom with 10 percent and Italy's Stet with 3.8 percent.</p>
<p>Iridium will be offering voice, paging and basic data services via portable phones and other equipment.</p>
<p>The announcement was made in Official Journal C255 of September 3.</p>
